cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KaryoDraw, please cite it as below."
title: "KaryoDraw: a zero-install browser tool that draws and explains ISCN karyotypes for genetics education"
abstract: "A free, client-side web tool that turns an ISCN 2024 karyotype into an annotated, correctly banded karyogram and a plain-language explanation of every symbol, for genetics and genetic-counseling education."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pique
    given-names: Daniel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0074-3974"
    affiliation: "StudyRare"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dpique/studyrare-karyodraw"
url: "https://karyodraw.com"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22119721"
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-08-27"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - genetics
  - cytogenetics
  - karyotype
  - ISCN
  - medical education
  - genetic counseling
# The doi above is the Zenodo *concept* DOI (10.5281/zenodo.22119721). It always
# resolves to the newest release, so a citation to it never goes stale. The v1.0.0
# snapshot has its own version DOI, 10.5281/zenodo.22119722; cite that one only when
# the exact archived version matters.
#
# When the JOSE paper is published, add it as a `preferred-citation:` block rather
# than replacing the doi above. The software archive and the paper are separate
# records with separate DOIs, and both should stay reachable from here.
